<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shakanda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1276</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shakanda was a king of Makuria in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>, installed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> in 1276. A relative of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">King David</a>, he sought the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a>, whose army defeated David near Dongola and placed Shakanda on the throne as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> bound by oath to pay an annual tribute. His accession marked the end of Makuria's independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>.</p></div>
